WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.400
In this video you’ll get your team onto the map.

2
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.601
Employees join with a site code.

3
00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:11.595
Managers get access by email.

4
00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:15.066
Open Sites & people.

5
00:00:15.517 --> 00:00:19.960
Every site has a six-character code, like this one for Sample Garage.

6
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.634
Give it to your employees.

7
00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:26.399
They sign in, type the code, and they can view that site’s published maps.

8
00:00:26.399 --> 00:00:28.137
They can’t change anything.

9
00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:31.952
If too many people have the code, choose New code.

10
00:00:31.952 --> 00:00:36.787
The old code stops working. People who already joined keep their access.

11
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.114
For managers, use Give someone access.

12
00:00:40.114 --> 00:00:41.778
Type their work email.

13
00:00:42.231 --> 00:00:47.577
Pick their access. A site manager can edit and publish maps at their own site.

14
00:00:47.577 --> 00:00:51.620
A regional manager can edit and publish maps at every site.

15
00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.402
An employee can only view.

16
00:00:53.852 --> 00:00:57.595
Pick the site, and choose Give access.

17
00:00:58.047 --> 00:01:00.524
The app does not send them an email.

18
00:01:00.524 --> 00:01:04.376
Choose Copy invite message and send it to them yourself.

19
00:01:04.376 --> 00:01:06.991
It has the link and the sign-in steps.

20
00:01:07.441 --> 00:01:10.917
Everyone with access is listed under People.

21
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:13.524
If someone leaves, choose Remove.

22
00:01:13.524 --> 00:01:15.736
They lose access right away.

23
00:01:16.187 --> 00:01:19.305
Here’s what joining looks like for a new employee.

24
00:01:19.305 --> 00:01:24.233
After they sign in, they type the code under Join a site, and choose Join site.

25
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.962
Sample Garage now shows up with its published map.

26
00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:32.708
They open it, search for a space, and choose Directions to see the way there.

27
00:01:35.063 --> 00:01:41.427
That’s it. Your map is built, published, and your team is on it.
